numbered 1..N, using 1-indexed, bridge N wraps).\n\nLet me use 0-indexed bridges 0..N-1 where bridge j connects (j+1) and (j+2) with wraparound... hmm let's stick with problem: bridge i connects i and i+1 for i=1..N-1, bridge N connects N and 1.\n\nSo going from a to a+1 uses bridge a (for a<N), from N to 1 uses bridge N. Going clockwise from a with step: pass bridges a, a+1, ..., wrapping.\n\nRange [a, a+cw_i-1] in mod-N arithmetic where bridges are 1..N. Let's convert to 0-indexed b' = a-1, length cw_i.\n\nUse diff array size N, add v to positions [start, start+len-1] mod N.\n\nThen answer = base + min over k of diff_sum[k].\n\nLet me code it.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    M = int(input_data[1])\n    X = [int(x) for x in input_data[2:2+M]]\n    \n    base = 0\n    diff = [0] * (N + 1)  # difference array for length N, indices 0..N-1\n    \n    for i in range(M - 1):\n        a = X[i]\n        b = X[i+1]\n        cw = (b - a) % N\n        base += cw\n        v = N - 2 * cw\n        # bridge range in 1-indexed: [a, a+cw-1] mod N, bridges 1..N\n        # convert to 0-indexed: start = a-1, length = cw\n        start = a - 1\n        length = cw\n        end = start + length - 1  # inclusive\n        if end < N:\n            diff[start] += v\n            diff[end + 1] -= v\n        else:\n            diff[start] += v\n            diff[N] -= v\n            diff[0] += v\n            diff[end - N + 1] -= v\n    \n    # compute prefix sum\n    best = float('inf')\n    cur = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        cur += diff[i]\n        if cur < best:\n            best = cur\n    \n    print(base + best)\n\nsolve()\n```",
