      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each section, enumerate the number of type-1 sensors used (0..ceil(D/L1)), then compute needed type-2. Minimize cost per section... but we have global constraints K1, K2.\n\nSo DP: for each section, possible (a, b) pairs where a*L1 + b*L2 >= D, a<=K1, b<=K2. Minimize total a's and b's subject to sum a <= K1, sum b <= K2.\n\nN up to 100, K up to 1000. DP state: after processing i sections, used a type-1 sensors, track min type-2 used. dp[i][a] = min b used. Then final answer: min over a,b of a*C1 + b*C2.\n\nFor each section, options: a1 from 0 to K1, need b such that a1*L1 + b*L2 >= D, b = max(0, ceil((D-a1*L1)/L2)). But we also want to allow using more b than needed? No, minimum is fine since more just costs more. But we might want fewer a and more b or vice versa - we enumerate a fully.\n\nActually to be safe, for each section enumerate all (a,b) with a in [0, min(K1, ceil(D/L1))] and b = required. That's optimal per section for that a.\n\nDP: dp[a_total] = min b_total. Initialize dp[0]=0. For each section, new_dp[a+a_i] = min(new_dp[a+a_i], dp[a] + b_i).\n\nSize: a_total up to K1=1000. Per section up to 1000 options × 1000 states = 10^6, times 100 sections = 10^8. Might be tight but ok in Python... let's optimize.\n\nActually a per section is bounded by ceil(D_i/L1) ≤ 10^5/1+1 which could be big, but we cap at K1=1000. Also b required must be ≤ K2. So valid options per section ≤ 1001.\n\nLet me code it.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    D = [int(input_data[idx+i]) for i in range(N)]\n    idx += N\n    L1 = int(input_data[idx]); C1 = int(input_data[idx+1]); K1 = int(input_data[idx+2])\n    idx += 3\n    L2 = int(input_data[idx]); C2 = int(input_data[idx+1]); K2 = int(input_data[idx+2])\n    \n    INF = float('inf')\n    # dp[a] = min b used across processed sections\n    dp = [INF] * (K1 + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for d in D:\n        new_dp = [INF] * (K1 + 1)\n        # enumerate options for this section\n        options = []\n        max_a = min(K1, (d + L1 - 1) // L1)\n        for a in range(0, max_a + 1):\n            covered = a * L1\n            if covered >= d:\n                b = 0\n            else:\n                b = (d - covered + L2 - 1) // L2\n            if b <= K2:\n                options.append((a, b))\n        if not options:\n            print(-1)\n            return\n        \n        for a_prev in range(K1 + 1):\n            if dp[a_prev] == INF:\n                continue\n            for (ai, bi) in options:\n                na = a_prev + ai\n                if na > K1:\n                    continue\n                nb = dp[a_prev] + bi\n                if nb < new_dp[na]:\n                    new_dp[na] = nb\n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    ans = INF\n    for a in range(K1 + 1):\n        if dp[a] != INF and dp[a] <= K2:\n            cost = a * C1 + dp[a] * C2\n            if cost < ans:\n                ans = cost\n    \n    print(-1 if ans == INF else ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
