      "generated_answer": "<think>\nSplit by '0'. For each segment, count 1s and 2s. Need logo tshirts >= 2s. Plain tshirts = M. In segment, 1s can use plain first, remaining 1s need logo. So logo needed = count2 + max(0, count1 - M). Take max over segments, subtract... wait need to buy = max needed - 0 (initially 0 logo). Actually answer = max over segments of (count2 + max(0, count1 - M)).\n\nWait but plain can also be used for 1. Total plain M. In segment, use min(count1, M) plain shirts for meals. Remaining count1 - that need logo. Plus count2 needs logo. So logo needed in segment = count2 + max(0, count1 - M). Answer = max of these.\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    M = int(input_data[1])\n    S = input_data[2]\n    \n    ans = 0\n    for segment in S.split('0'):\n        c1 = segment.count('1')\n        c2 = segment.count('2')\n        need = c2 + max(0, c1 - M)\n        ans = max(ans, need)\n    print(ans)\n\nsolve()\n```",
