      "generated_answer": "<analysis>\nWe need to try all offsets of A and B relative to X such that all black squares of A and B fall within the X window, and the union matches X exactly.\n\nLet me place X at origin. A's top-left at (da, db_col), B's at similar. Actually simpler: iterate offset of B relative to A, then offset of window relative to A.\n\nRange of offsets: since sizes ≤10, we can iterate offsets from -20 to 20.\n\nLet me place A at position (0,0). B's top-left at (bi, bj) where bi, bj in range say -10..20. Window top-left at (xi, xj). Check all A blacks are in window, all B blacks in window, and window content equals X.\n\nActually easier: iterate window position (xi, xj) — the offset from A's origin. Window covers rows xi..xi+HX-1, cols xj..xj+WX-1. All A's black squares must be inside window. Then iterate B's offset (bi,bj), all B's black must be inside window. Then check for each cell in window, black iff X says black.\n\nRanges: xi from -HX to HA (roughly), similar for others. Let's just use -20..20.\n</analysis>\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    HA, WA = int(input_data[idx]), int(input_data[idx+1]); idx+=2\n    A = [input_data[idx+i] for i in range(HA)]; idx+=HA\n    HB, WB = int(input_data[idx]), int(input_data[idx+1]); idx+=2\n    B = [input_data[idx+i] for i in range(HB)]; idx+=HB\n    HX, WX = int(input_data[idx]), int(input_data[idx+1]); idx+=2\n    X = [input_data[idx+i] for i in range(HX)]; idx+=HX\n    \n    A_blacks = [(i,j) for i in range(HA) for j in range(WA) if A[i][j]=='#']\n    B_blacks = [(i,j) for i in range(HB) for j in range(WB) if B[i][j]=='#']\n    \n    # A placed at (0,0) on sheet C. Window top-left at (xi,xj). B top-left at (bi,bj).\n    R = 25\n    for xi in range(-R, R+1):\n        for xj in range(-R, R+1):\n            # all A blacks must be in window\n            ok = True\n            for (i,j) in A_blacks:\n                if not (xi <= i < xi+HX and xj <= j < xj+WX):\n                    ok = False; break\n            if not ok: continue\n            for bi in range(-R, R+1):\n                for bj in range(-R, R+1):\n                    ok2 = True\n                    for (i,j) in B_blacks:\n                        ai, aj = i+bi, j+bj\n                        if not (xi <= ai < xi+HX and xj <= aj < xj+WX):\n                            ok2 = False; break\n                    if not ok2: continue\n                    # build window\n                    match = True\n                    for r in range(HX):\n                        for c in range(WX):\n                            ar, ac = xi+r, xj+c\n                            black = False\n                            if 0 <= ar < HA and 0 <= ac < WA and A[ar][ac]=='#':\n                                black = True\n                            br, bc = ar-bi, ac-bj\n                            if 0 <= br < HB and 0 <= bc < WB and B[br][bc]=='#':\n                                black = True\n                            want = X[r][c]=='#'\n                            if black != want:\n                                match = False; break\n                        if not match: break\n                    if match:\n                        print(\"Yes\")\n                        return\n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
