id = [-1]*(101*101)\n```\n\nLet me refine:\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx]); idx+=1\n    cub = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        cub.append(tuple(int(x) for x in data[idx:idx+6]))\n        idx += 6\n    \n    neighbors = [set() for _ in range(N)]\n    grid = [-1]*(101*101)\n    \n    for axis in range(3):\n        a1 = (axis+1)%3\n        a2 = (axis+2)%3\n        min_group = [[] for _ in range(101)]\n        max_group = [[] for _ in range(101)]\n        for i in range(N):\n            c = cub[i]\n            min_group[c[axis]].append(i)\n            max_group[c[axis+3]].append(i)\n        \n        for v in range(101):\n            mg = min_group[v]\n            xg = max_group[v]\n            if not mg or not xg:\n                continue\n            touched = []\n            for i in xg:\n                c = cub[i]\n                for p in range(c[a1], c[a1+3]):\n                    base = p*101\n                    for q in range(c[a2], c[a2+3]):\n                        grid[base+q] = i\n                        touched.append(base+q)\n            for i in mg:\n                c = cub[i]\n                seen = set()\n                for p in range(c[a1], c[a1+3]):\n                    base = p*101\n                    for q in range(c[a2], c[a2+3]):\n                        j = grid[base+q]\n                        if j != -1:\n                            seen.add(j)\n                for j in seen:\n                    neighbors[i].add(j)\n                    neighbors[j].add(i)\n            for t in touched:\n                grid[t] = -1\n    \n    out = '\\n'.join(str(len(s)) for s in neighbors)\n    sys.stdout.write(out+'\\n')\n\nsolve()\n```\n\nHmm, `touched` might have duplicates if max_group rects overlapped, but they shouldn't (non-overlapping in volume => rects don't overlap in yz for same plane... wait). \n\nFor max_group at plane v (axis=x): cuboids have X2=v.