      "generated_answer": "<think>\nCells adjacent to magnet are \"blocked\" - can't move. From free cells (no magnet adjacent), BFS through free cells, counting all cells visited (including blocked non-magnet cells reached).\n\nStandard approach: BFS from each free cell, but with connected components. Free cells form components; blocked non-magnet cells are boundary — they can be reached but you stop there.\n\nSo for each connected component of \"free\" cells (cells with no adjacent magnet, connected via adjacency), the reachable set = free cells in component + all non-magnet neighbors of any free cell in component.\n\nUse BFS/union: for each free cell, mark component. Then for each component, count free cells + adjacent non-magnet cells (but same non-magnet cell might be counted from multiple free cells in same component — dedupe).\n\nImplementation: assign component id via BFS on free cells. For each component, use a set or mark visited with component id... Actually a non-magnet blocked cell can be adjacent to multiple free cells possibly in same component. Need to count unique.\n\nApproach: for each component, BFS: start from any free cell, do BFS. When at a free cell, expand to neighbors (any non-magnet). If neighbor is free, continue BFS. If neighbor is blocked non-magnet, add to count but don't expand. Use visited set per component.\n\nBut visited set — a blocked cell might belong to multiple components. So we need per-component visited. Use a timestamp/component id array for \"last visited component\".\n\nLet me code it:\n\n- Compute is_free[i][j] = cell is '.' and no adjacent '#'\n- comp[i][j] = component id via BFS on free cells\n- For each component, do BFS: count = 0, use a \"seen\" marker. Start with free cells of component. For each free cell (already in component), add to count. Then check its neighbors — non-magnet neighbors that are not free cells (i.e., blocked non-magnet). Add them if not seen this component.\n\nActually simpler: for each component id c, iterate through all free cells with comp==c, count them, and collect their non-magnet neighbors into a set (excluding free cells themselves since they're counted). Then answer = free_count + len(neighbor_set).\n\nWait, free cells are also non-magnet. Neighbor of a free cell that's also free is in same component. So:\n- total = (number of free cells in component) + (number of blocked-non-magnet cells adjacent to any free cell in component, deduped)\n\nLet's use a \"last_comp_seen\" array for blocked cells to dedupe.\n\nAlso special case: an isolated '.' cell that's blocked (has adjacent magnet) — it's not free, so no component contains it as a free cell. But it should have degree of freedom = 1. So answer must be at least 1 if any non-magnet cell exists.\n\nLet me code:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    H = int(input_data[0]); W = int(input_data[1])\n    grid = [input_data[2+i].decode() for i in range(H)]\n    \n    is_magnet = [[c=='#' for c in row] for row in grid]\n    is_free = [[False]*W for _ in range(H)]\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if is_magnet[i][j]: continue\n            free = True\n            for di,dj in ((-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)):\n                ni,nj = i+di, j+dj\n                if 0<=ni<H and 0<=nj<W and is_magnet[ni][nj]:\n                    free = False; break\n            is_free[i][j] = free\n    \n    comp = [[-1]*W for _ in range(H)]\n    ans = 1  # at least 1 since there's a non-magnet cell\n    cid = 0\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if is_free[i][j] and comp[i][j]==-1:\n                # BFS\n                q = deque([(i,j)])\n                comp[i][j] = cid\n                cells = []\n                while q:\n                    x,y = q.popleft()\n                    cells.append((x,y))\n                    for dx,dy in ((-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)):\n                        nx,ny = x+dx,y+dy\n                        if 0<=nx<H and 0<=ny<W and is_free[nx][ny] and comp[nx][ny]==-1:\n                            comp[nx][ny] = cid\n                            q.append((nx,ny))\n                # count reachable\n                total = len(cells)\n                # blocked non-magnet neighbors\n                seen = set()\n                for x,y in cells:\n                    for dx,dy in ((-1,0),(1,0),(0,-1),(0,1)):\n                        nx,ny = x+dx,y+dy\n                        if 0<=nx<H and 0<=ny<W and not is_magnet[nx][ny] and not is_free[nx][ny]:\n                            if (nx,ny) not in seen:\n                                seen.add((nx,ny))\n                                total += 1\n                if total > ans: ans = total\n                cid += 1\n    \n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```\n\nFor H,W=1000, 10^6 cells. Using set of tuples might be slow. Use a 2D last_seen array instead.\n\nLet me optimize with a flat array.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    H = int(data[0]); W = int(data[1])\n    grid = [data[2+i].decode() for i in range(H)]\n    \n    N = H * W\n    is_magnet = bytearray(N)\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = grid[i]\n        base = i * W\n        for j in range(W):\n            if row[j] == '#':\n                is_magnet[base+j] = 1\n    \n    is_free = bytearray(N)\n    for i in range(H):\n        base = i * W\n        for j in range(W):\n            idx = base + j\n            if is_magnet[idx]:\n                continue\n            free = 1\n            if i > 0 and is_magnet[idx-W]: free = 0\n            elif i < H-1 and is_magnet[idx+W]: free = 0\n            elif j > 0 and is_magnet[idx-1]: free = 0\n            elif j < W-1 and is_magnet[idx+1]: free = 0\n            is_free[idx] = free\n    \n    comp = [-1] * N\n    last_seen = [-1] * N  # for blocked non-magnet cells\n    ans = 1\n    cid = 0\n    \n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            start = i * W + j\n            if is_free[start] and comp[start] == -1:\n                q = deque([start])\n                comp[start] = cid\n                cells = []\n                while q:\n                    idx = q.popleft()\n                    cells.append(idx)\n                    x, y = divmod(idx, W)\n                    if x > 0:\n                        n = idx - W\n                        if is_free[n] and comp[n] == -1:\n                            comp[n] = cid; q.append(n)\n                    if x < H-1:\n                        n = idx + W\n                        if is_free[n] and comp[n] == -1:\n                            comp[n] = cid; q.append(n)\n                    if y > 0:\n                        n = idx - 1\n                        if is_free[n] and comp[n] == -1:\n                            comp[n] = cid; q.append(n)\n                    if y < W-1:\n                        n = idx + 1\n                        if is_free[n] and comp[n] == -1:\n                            comp[n] = cid; q.append(n)\n                \n                total = len(cells)\n                for idx in cells:\n                    x, y = divmod(idx, W)\n                    if x > 0:\n                        n = idx - W\n                        if not is_magnet[n] and not is_free[n] and last_seen[n] != cid:\n                            last_seen[n] = cid; total += 1\n                    if x < H-1:\n                        n = idx + W\n                        if not is_magnet[n] and not is_free[n] and last_seen[n] != cid:\n                            last_seen[n] = cid; total += 1\n                    if y > 0:\n                        n = idx - 1\n                        if not is_magnet[n] and not is_free[n] and last_seen[n] != cid:\n                            last_seen[n] = cid; total += 1\n                    if y < W-1:\n                        n = idx + 1\n                        if not is_magnet[n] and not is_free[n] and last_seen[n] != cid:\n                            last_seen[n] = cid; total += 1\n                \n                if total > ans: ans = total\n                cid += 1\n    \n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
