y_1 = 5. Therefore, print No.\n- For the second question, the graph G^{{(2)}} is not good because it has a path 2 \\rightarrow 6 connecting vertices x_2 = 2 and y_2 = 6. Therefore, print No.\n- For the third question, the graph G^{{(3)}} is good. Therefore, print Yes.\n- For the fourth question, the graph G^{{(4)}} is good. Therefore, print Yes.\n\nAs seen in this sample input, note that the given graph G may have self-loops or multi-edges.",
    "prediction": "claude-opus-4-7",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each query (p,q), adding edge merges components of p and q (if different). Need to check: for all K constraints, no x_i,y_i become connected. That means: no constraint has {comp(x_i), comp(y_i)} = {comp(p), comp(q)}.\n\nGroup constraints by unordered pair of components. For query, get comp(p), comp(q). If same, answer Yes (no new connectivity). Otherwise check if pair exists in set.\n\nUse DSU, then store set of frozensets or tuples (min,max).\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom sys import setrecursionlimit\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    \n    parent = list(range(N+1))\n    rank_ = [0]*(N+1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x,y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry: return\n        if rank_[rx] < rank_[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank_[rx] == rank_[ry]:\n            rank_[rx] += 1\n    \n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        v = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        union(u,v)\n    \n    K = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    forbidden = set()\n    for _ in range(K):\n        x = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        y = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        a, b = find(x), find(y)\n        if a > b: a,b = b,a\n        forbidden.add((a,b))\n    \n    Q = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    out = []\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        p = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        q = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        a, b = find(p), find(q)\n        if a == b:\n            out.append(\"Yes\")\n        else:\n            if a > b: a,b = b,a\n            if (a,b) in forbidden:\n                out.append(\"No\")\n            else:\n                out.append(\"Yes\")\n    \n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(out))\n\nmain()\n```",
