t some point. Then y not paid.\n\nSo q_y = P(first roll that is >= y equals y, considering only \"effective\" rolls before termination).\n\nHmm, but termination can happen from rolls <y. Let me reconsider.\n\nLet's think differently. At any point, consider condition x<y. Initially true. We keep rolling. The event \"y is paid\" is: eventually we roll y while x<y.\n\nGiven x<y currently. Roll a value r uniform 1..N.\n- r=y: pay y. Success.\n- r>y: then x<y<r, we pay r, x=r>=y, from now on x>=y forever. Failure for y.\n- x<r<y: pay r, x=r, still x<y. Continue.\n- r<=x: terminate. Failure.\n- r=x: terminate (r<=x). But r<y still.\n\nHmm wait when x<r<y we pay r and continue with x=r. When r<=x, terminate.\n\nSo we need probability that starting from x=0, we reach state where we roll y before rolling anything >y or rolling <=current x.\n\nLet f(x) = P(y paid | current state x, x<y). We want f(0).\n\nFrom state x (x<y): roll uniform 1..N.\n- r = y (prob 1/N): success\n- r > y (prob (N-y)/N): failure\n- x < r < y (prob (y-1-x)/N): continue from state r\n- r <= x (prob x/N): failure\n\nf(x) = 1/N + sum_{r=x+1}^{y-1} f(r)/N\n\nLet S(x) = sum_{r=x+1}^{y-1} f(r). Then f(x) = (1 + S(x))/N.\n\nf(y-1) = 1/N.\nf(y-2) = (1 + f(y-1))/N = (1+1/N)/N\nf(y-3) = (1 + f(y-2) + f(y-1))/N\n\nLet g(x) = f(x) for x=0..y-1. g(y-1) = 1/N.\ng(x) = (1 + sum_{r=x+1}^{y-1} g(r))/N.\n\ng(x-1) - g(x) = ? g(x-1) = (1 + g(x) + sum_{r=x+1}^{y-1} g(r))/N = g(x) + g(x)/... wait:\ng(x-1) = (1 + sum_{r=x}^{y-1} g(r))/N = (1 + g(x) + sum_{r=x+1}^{y-1} g(r))/N\n     = g(x) + g(x)/N... hmm, g(x)*N = 1 + sum_{r=x+1}^{y-1} g(r), so\ng(x-1) = (1 + g(x) + g(x)*N - 1)/N = g(x)(N+1)/N.\n\nSo g(x-1) = g(x) * (N+1)/N.\n\nSo g(0) = g(y-1) * ((N+1)/N)^{y-1} = (1/N) * ((N+1)/N)^{y-1}.\n\nSo q_y = (N+1)^{y-1} / N^y.\n\nAnswer = sum_{y=1}^N A_y * (N+1)^{y-1} / N^y mod p.\n\nLet me verify with sample 1: N=3, A=[3,2,6].\nq_1 = 1/3\nq_2 = 4/9\nq_3 = 16/27\nE = 3*(1/3) + 2*(4/9) + 6*(16/27) = 1 + 8/9 + 96/27 = 27/27 + 24/27 + 96/27 = 147/27 = 49/9. ✓\n\nGreat.\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    A = [int(x) for x in input_data[1:1+N]]\n    MOD = 998244353\n    inv_N = pow(N, MOD-2, MOD)\n    r = (N + 1) * inv_N % MOD  # (N+1)/N\n    # q_y = (1/N) * r^(y-1)\n    ans = 0\n    cur = inv_N  # for y=1: q_1 = 1/N\n    for y in range(1, N+1):\n        ans = (ans + A[y-1] * cur) % MOD\n        cur = cur * r % MOD\n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
