      "generated_answer": "<think>\nD_i mod (A+B), need all fall in [1,A] after adding offset x where x in [0, A+B-1] representing today's position... Let today be day t (1..A+B). Then D_i days later is ((t-1+D_i) mod (A+B))+1. Need this in [1,A], i.e., (t-1+D_i) mod (A+B) in [0,A-1].\n\nLet r_i = D_i mod (A+B). We need t-1+r_i mod W in [0,A-1]. Let s = t-1, s in [0,W-1]. Need (s+r_i) mod W < A for all i.\n\nSort r_i. For each i, s must be in [(-r_i) mod W, (-r_i + A -1) mod W]. Intersection of these intervals on circle.\n\nSimpler: compute mods, sort. Let m = min, M = max of r_i. Then max-min < A works if we pick s = W - m (so smallest becomes 0). Actually if max - min <= A-1, then choose s such that s+min ≡ 0, then s+max = max-min < A. Yes.\n\nBut circular: could also work if the values are clustered. Sort r_i, find max gap between consecutive (circular). If W - gap <= A-1... wait, span = W - maxGap. Need span <= A-1.\n\nWait: after sorting r_i in [0,W-1], the \"span\" needed to cover them is W - maxGap where maxGap is the largest gap between consecutive (including wrap around from last to first + W). If span <= A-1 (i.e., span+1 <= A), then answer Yes.\n\nLet me verify sample 1: W=7, D=1,2,9 → r=1,2,2. Sorted: 1,2,2. Gaps: 1, 0, and wrap: 7-2+1=6. Max gap=6. Span=7-6=1. Need span<=A-1=1. Yes.\n\nSample 2: W=15, r=10,0. Sorted: 0,10. Gaps: 10, 5. Max=10. Span=5. A-1=4. 5>4, No. ✓\n\nSample 3: W=694, A=347. r: 347, 700%694=6, 705%694=11, 710%694=16. Sorted: 6,11,16,347. Gaps:5,5,331, wrap 694-347+6=353. Max=353. Span=694-353=341. A-1=346. 341<=346. Yes. ✓\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(input_data[0]); A = int(input_data[1]); B = int(input_data[2])\n    W = A + B\n    r = sorted(int(x) % W for x in input_data[3:3+N])\n    if N == 1:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        return\n    max_gap = 0\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        max_gap = max(max_gap, r[i] - r[i-1])\n    max_gap = max(max_gap, W