      "generated_answer": "<think>\nTransform (x,y) -> (u,v) = (x+y, x-y). Then jumps change u by ±2 and v by ±2 independently... wait, jump (x+1,y+1): u+=2, v+=0. (x+1,y-1): u+=0, v+=2. (x-1,y+1): u+=0, v-=2. (x-1,y-1): u-=2, v+=0. So each jump changes exactly one of u,v by ±2.\n\nDistance = max(|du|/2, |dv|/2)... no wait, each jump changes one coordinate by 2. So min jumps = |du|/2 + |dv|/2? No, in Chebyshev after transform... Let me reconsider.\n\nActually the original jump moves: it's like king moves diagonal. In (u,v) coordinates, each jump moves either u or v by ±2. So it's Manhattan distance in (u,v)/2.\n\nWait but this only works if parity of x+y is preserved. x+y changes by 0 or ±2, so parity of x+y preserved. So reachable iff (x_A+y_A) and (x_B+y_B) have same parity.\n\nDistance = (|du| + |dv|)/2 where du = (x_B+y_B)-(x_A+y_A), dv = (x_B-y_B)-(x_A-y_A).\n\nNote du = (xB-xA)+(yB-yA), dv = (xB-xA)-(yB-yA). |du|+|dv| = 2*max(|xB-xA|, |yB-yA|).\n\nSo dist = max(|dx|, |dy|) when parities match, else 0.\n\nSo we need sum over pairs with same parity of x+y of max(|xi-xj|, |yi-yj|).\n\nSplit points by parity of x+y. For each group, compute sum of max(|dx|, |dy|) over pairs.\n\nmax(|dx|,|dy|) = (|dx+dy| + |dx-dy|)/2 = (|du|+|dv|)/2 where u=x+y, v=x-y.\n\nSo compute for each group: sum over pairs of (|u_i-u_j| + |v_i-v_j|)/2.\n\nThis is standard: sort u's, sum of |ui-uj| = sum over sorted i of u_i*(i - (n-1-i)) etc.\n\nLet me code it.\n\nFor sorted array a[0..n-1], sum of pairwise |ai-aj| = sum_i a[i]*i - a[i]*(n-1-i) = sum_i a[i]*(2i - (n-1)).\n\nThen answer = (sumU + sumV) / 2 for each group, summed.\n\nLet me verify with sample 1:\nPoints: (0,0),(1,3),(5,6). Parities of x+y: 0, 4(even), 11(odd). So P1,P2 in even group, P3 in odd.\nFor P1,P2: max(|0-1|,|0-3|) = 3. ✓\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    groups = {0: [], 1: []}\n    idx = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        x = int(input_data[idx]); y = int(input_data[idx+1])\n        idx += 2\n        p = (x + y) & 1\n        groups[p].append((x + y, x - y))\n    \n    total = 0\n    for pts in groups.values():\n        m = len(pts)\n        if m < 2:\n            continue\n        us = sorted(p[0] for p in pts)\n        vs = sorted(p[1] for p in pts)\n        s_u = 0\n        s_v = 0\n        for i in range(m):\n            s_u += us[i] * (2*i - (m-1))\n            s_v += vs[i] * (2*i - (m-1))\n        total += (s_u + s_v) // 2\n    print(total)\n\nsolve()\n```",
