      "generated_answer": "<think>\nPrefix sum of sleep. sleep intervals [A[2i-1], A[2i]] for i=1..(N-1)/2, wait indices: A_2 fell asleep, A_3 woke up. So sleep=[A_2,A_3],[A_4,A_5],...\n\nDefine f(t) = total sleep time in [0,t]. For a query (l,r), answer = f(r)-f(l).\n\nTo compute f(t): find where t falls. Binary search in array A. Let idx = number of elements <= t... Let me think: precompute prefix sleep P[k] = total sleep in [0, A_k].\n\nP[1]=0. For k>=2: if k even, P[k]=P[k-1] (awake from A[k-1] to A[k]). If k odd, P[k]=P[k-1]+(A[k]-A[k-1]).\n\nFor time t, find largest k with A[k]<=t. Then:\n- if k is odd (awake state after A[k]), f(t) = P[k].\n- if k is even (asleep after A[k]), f(t) = P[k] + (t - A[k]).\n\nUsing 1-indexed. In Python use 0-indexed: A[0]=0 corresponds to A_1. So position i (0-indexed) is odd-numbered (1-indexed) if i is even.\n\nLet me redo with 0-indexed. A[0], A[1], ..., A[N-1]. Sleep intervals: [A[1],A[2]], [A[3],A[4]], ...\n\nP[i] = total sleep in [0, A[i]]. P[0]=0. For i>=1: if i is odd, sleeping between A[i-1] and A[i]? No wait: A[1] is falling asleep. So [A[1],A[2]] is sleep. So between A[0] and A[1] awake, between A[1] and A[2] sleep, etc.\n\nSo segment (A[i-1], A[i]) is sleep if i is even (i>=2), awake if i is odd.\n\nP[i] = P[i-1] + (A[i]-A[i-1]) if i even, else P[i-1].\n\nFor time t, find largest i with A[i]<=t (via bisect_right - 1). Then t is in segment (A[i], A[i+1]). This segment is sleep if i+1 is even, i.e., i is odd. So:\n- if i odd: f(t) = P[i] + (t - A[i])\n- if i even: f(t) = P[i]\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom bisect import bisect_right\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx]); idx += 1\n    A = [int(data[idx+i]) for i in range(N)]\n    idx += N\n    P = [0]*N\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            P[i] = P[i-1] + (A[i]-A[i-1])\n        else:\n            P[i] = P[i-1]\n    \n    def f(t):\n        i = bisect_right(A, t) - 1\n        if