      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each j, count number of i≤j with f(i,j)=1. Let c1[j] = count of i in [1,j] with f(i,j)=1, c0[j] = count with f(i,j)=0.\n\nTransition: f(i,j) = f(i,j-1) NAND A[j].\nIf A[j]=0: NAND with 0 always gives 1. So all f(i,j-1) become 1 for i<j. Plus f(j,j)=A[j]=0.\nSo c1[j] = (j-1) + 0 = j-1, c0[j] = 1.\n\nIf A[j]=1: NAND with 1: 0→1, 1→0. So c1[j] from prev c0, c0[j] from prev c1. Plus f(j,j)=1.\nSo c1[j] = c0[j-1] + 1, c0[j] = c1[j-1].\n\nSum c1[j].\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    s = data[1]\n    ans = 0\n    c0 = 0\n    c1 = 0\n    for ch in s:\n        if ch == '0':\n            new_c1 = c0 + c1  # = j-1\n            new_c0 = 1\n        else:\n            new_c1 = c0 + 1\n            new_c0 = c1\n        c0, c1 = new_c0, new_c1\n        ans += c1\n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
