      "generated_answer": "<think>\nM = ceil(log2(N)). Friend i gets bottles where bit i is set in (bottle number). Then S read as binary gives the bottle. Need to ensure bottle number in [1,N]. Use bit representation of the bottle index. If X=0 result... need to handle. Standard: assign each bottle a unique non-zero M-bit code. With M=ceil(log2(N)), we have 2^M >= N codes from 0 to 2^M-1, but if result is 0 (no one sick), that would mean bottle with code 0. So map bottle k (1..N) to code k, but need code != 0 possibly — well bottle 1 has code 1, ..., that's fine. If all S are 0, then... it means no friend got sick, meaning the bad bottle wasn't given to anyone. But every bottle from 1 to N has at least one bit set (since >=1), so code 0 won't occur. Good.\n\nWait, but we need M minimal. For N=2, M=1. Bottle 1 code=1 (bit 0 set), bottle 2 code=2 — but 2 in binary needs 2 bits. Hmm.\n\nBetter: assign codes 1..N in binary with M=ceil(log2(N+1))? For N=2: need codes to distinguish 2 bottles + possibility of \"all 0\". Actually with M friends, results are 2^M possible outcomes. Need 2^M >= N. For N=2, M=1: outcomes {0,1}, map bottle1->0, bottle2->1. But bottle mapped to 0 means giving it to no one, then S=\"0\" → bottle 1. That works! S=\"1\" → bottle 2 got by friend 1.\n\nSo use codes 0..N-1 for bottles 1..N. M = ceil(log2(N)).\n\nFor N=2, M=1. Bottle 1 → code 0 (given to nobody), bottle 2 → code 1 (given to friend 1). Friend 1 gets bottle 2. If S=1, answer 2; if S=0, answer 1. ✓\n\nNeed to flush output.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin\n    N = int(input_data.readline())\n    \n    # Minimum M such that 2^M >= N\n    M = 1\n    while (1 << M) < N:\n        M += 1\n    \n    print(M, flush=True)\n    \n    # Bottle i (1..N) gets code i-1\n    # Friend j (0..M-1) receives all bottles whose code has bit j set\n    for j in range(M):\n        bottles = []\n        for i in range(1, N + 1):\n            code = i - 1\n            if (code >> j) & 1:\n                bottles.append(i)\n        line = str(len(bottles))\n        if bottles:\n            line += \" \" + \" \".join(map(str, bottles))\n        print(line, flush=True)\n    \n    S = input_data.readline().strip()\n    # S[i] = '1' means friend i got sick, meaning bad bottle has bit i set\n    code = 0\n    for j in range(M):\n        if S[j] == '1':\n            code |= (1 << j)\n    \n    print(code + 1, flush=True)\n\nmain()\n```",
