      "generated_answer": "<think>\nStandard problem. Use memoization with dict. For die roll, b=1 makes N unchanged, so:\nE_die(N) = Y + (1/6)*sum(f(N//b) for b=1..6)\n= Y + (1/6)*f(N) + (1/6)*sum(f(N//b) for b=2..6)\nSo (5/6)*f_die contribution... Actually we compute:\noption2 = (Y + (1/6)*sum_{b=2..6} f(N//b)) / (5/6) = (6Y + sum_{b=2..6} f(N//b))/5\n\nf(N) = min(X + f(N//A), option2)\nf(0) = 0\n\nMemoize with dict. N reduces fast so state space is small.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\ndef main():\n    N, A, X, Y = map(int, sys.stdin.read().split())\n    memo = {}\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n    \n    def f(n):\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        if n in memo:\n            return memo[n]\n        op1 = X + f(n // A)\n        s = 0.0\n        for b in range(2, 7):\n            s += f(n // b)\n        op2 = (6 * Y + s) / 5.0\n        res = min(op1, op2)\n        memo[n] = res\n        return res\n    \n    print(f\"{f(N):.15f}\")\n\nmain()\n```",
