      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getMaxFunctionValue(receiver, k):\n    n = len(receiver)\n    LOG = k.bit_length()\n    # up[j][i] = 2^j-th ancestor of i\n    # sm[j][i] = sum of ids over 2^j steps starting from receiver[i]... \n    # Let's define: jump[j][i] = node after 2^j passes from i\n    # sum[j][i] = sum of receiver IDs collected during those 2^j passes (not including i)\n    jump = [receiver[:]]\n    sm = [receiver[:]]\n    for j in range(1, LOG + 1):\n        prev_j = jump[j-1]\n        prev_s = sm[j-1]\n        new_j = [0] * n\n        new_s = [0] * n\n        for i in range(n):\n            mid = prev_j[i]\n            new_j[i] = prev_j[mid]\n            new_s[i] = prev_s[i] + prev_s[mid]\n        jump.append(new_j)\n        sm.append(new_s)\n    \n    ans = 0\n    for x in range(n):\n        total = x\n        cur = x\n        kk = k\n        j = 0\n        while kk:\n            if kk & 1:\n                total += sm[j][cur]\n                cur = jump[j][cur]\n            kk >>= 1\n            j += 1\n        if total > ans:\n            ans = total\n    return ans\n```",
