      "generated_answer": "<think>\nBinary search on answer. Count numbers ≤ x that are multiple of any coin using inclusion-exclusion.\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef findKthSmallest(coins, k):\n    from math import gcd\n    from itertools import combinations\n    \n    n = len(coins)\n    \n    # Precompute LCMs for all subsets via inclusion-exclusion\n    subsets = []  # (lcm, sign)\n    for r in range(1, n + 1):\n        for combo in combinations(coins, r):\n            l = 1\n            for c in combo:\n                l = l * c // gcd(l, c)\n                if l > 10**18:\n                    break\n            sign = 1 if r % 2 == 1 else -1\n            subsets.append((l, sign))\n    \n    def count(x):\n        total = 0\n        for l, s in subsets:\n            total += s * (x // l)\n        return total\n    \n    lo, hi = 1, min(coins) * k\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if count(mid) >= k:\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    return lo\n```",
