      "generated_answer": "<think>\nBinary search on ratio r. Check if there's a path from 1 to N with sum(b - r*c) >= 0. Since u<v, DAG topological order is just vertex order. Max path DP.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom sys import stdin\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    edges = []\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N+1)]\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        v = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        b = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        c = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        adj[u].append((v,b,c))\n    \n    NEG = float('-inf')\n    \n    def check(r):\n        dp = [NEG]*(N+1)\n        dp[1] = 0.0\n        for u in range(1, N+1):\n            if dp[u] == NEG:\n                continue\n            for v,b,c in adj[u]:\n                w = b - r*c\n                if dp[u] + w > dp[v]:\n                    dp[v] = dp[u] + w\n        return dp[N] >= 0\n    \n    lo, hi = 0.0, 10000.0\n    for _ in range(100):\n        mid = (lo+hi)/2\n        if check(mid):\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    print(f\"{lo:.16f}\")\n\nmain()\n```",
