      "generated_answer": "<think>\nStandard bitmask DP for maximum weight matching on N≤16.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    D = [[0]*N for _ in range(N)]\n    for i in range(N-1):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            D[i][j] = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n            D[j][i] = D[i][j]\n    \n    size = 1 << N\n    dp = [0] * size\n    for mask in range(size):\n        # find lowest unset... actually find lowest set bit i, then try pair with j\n        # standard: find first bit i, either skip or match with some j\n        i = -1\n        for b in range(N):\n            if mask & (1 << b):\n                i = b\n                break\n        if i == -1:\n            continue\n        # option 1: leave i unmatched\n        dp[mask] = dp[mask ^ (1 << i)]\n        # option 2: match i with j\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            if mask & (1 << j):\n                val = dp[mask ^ (1 << i) ^ (1 << j)] + D[i][j]\n                if val > dp[mask]:\n                    dp[mask] = val\n    \n    print(dp[size - 1])\n\nsolve()\n```",
