      "generated_answer": "<think>\nGreedy: cover [L, R+1) with largest possible power-of-2 blocks aligned. Standard approach.\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.readline().split()\n    N, L, R = int(input_data[0]), int(input_data[1]), int(input_data[2])\n    \n    total = 0\n    l = L\n    r = R + 1  # exclusive\n    \n    while l < r:\n        # find largest i such that l is divisible by 2^i and l + 2^i <= r\n        i = 0\n        while l % (1 << (i+1)) == 0 and l + (1 << (i+1)) <= r:\n            i += 1\n        j = l >> i\n        print(f\"? {i} {j}\", flush=True)\n        t = int(sys.stdin.readline())\n        if t == -1:\n            sys.exit(0)\n        total = (total + t) % 100\n        l += (1 << i)\n    \n    print(f\"! {total}\", flush=True)\n\nsolve()\n```",
