      "generated_answer": "<think>\ndp[i][j][k] where k is last element. Let f(z,o,last) = number of arrays using z zeros and o ones ending with last. Transition: consider how many of the last element at the end (block size 1..limit).\n\nf(z,o,0) = sum_{i=1..min(limit,z)} f(z-i, o, 1), with base when z-i==0 and o==0 means empty... Actually the block of i zeros preceded by arrays ending in 1 (or empty if that's the whole array).\n\nLet me define f(z,o,last) = arrays with exactly z zeros, o ones, ending in `last`. \nf(z,o,0) = sum_{i=1..min(limit,z)} [f(z-i, o, 1) + (z-i==0 and o==0 ? 1 : 0)]\nSimilarly for 1.\n\nBase: f(0,0,*) = 0 but we handle empty prefix specially.\n\nAnswer = f(zero, one, 0) + f(zero, one, 1).\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef numberOfStableArrays(zero, one, limit):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    from functools import lru_cache\n    \n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def f(z, o, last):\n        # arrays with exactly z zeros, o ones, ending in `last` (0 or 1)\n        if last == 0:\n            if z == 0:\n                return 0\n            total = 0\n            for i in range(1, min(limit, z) + 1):\n                # place i zeros at end, prefix has z-i zeros, o ones, ends in 1 (or empty)\n                if z - i == 0 and o == 0:\n                    total += 1\n                else:\n                    total += f(z - i, o, 1)\n            return total % MOD\n        else:\n            if o == 0:\n                return 0\n            total = 0\n            for i in range(1, min(limit, o) + 1):\n                if o - i == 0 and z == 0:\n                    total += 1\n                else:\n                    total += f(z, o - i, 0)\n            return total % MOD\n    \n    return (f(zero, one, 0) + f(zero, one, 1)) % MOD\n```",
