    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nSort by a_i. Binary search on day X: sum of b_i where a_i >= X <= K. Find smallest X.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    K = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    meds = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        a = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        b = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        meds.append((a, b))\n    meds.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    a_list = [m[0] for m in meds]\n    b_list = [m[1] for m in meds]\n    # suffix sum of b\n    total = sum(b_list)\n    # prefix sum\n    prefix = [0]*(N+1)\n    for i in range(N):\n        prefix[i+1] = prefix[i] + b_list[i]\n    # For day X, medicines still active: those with a_i >= X. In sorted order, find first index where a_i >= X.\n    # Sum = total - prefix[idx]\n    # We want smallest X >= 1 such that total - prefix[idx(X)] <= K\n    # Binary search X in [1, max_a+1]\n    lo, hi = 1, a_list[-1] + 1\n    import bisect\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        i = bisect.bisect_left(a_list, mid)\n        s = total - prefix[i]\n        if s <= K:\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    print(lo)\n\nmain()\n```",
