    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each piece on vertex x, we want to maximize operations. Each operation on x gives 1 + (max ops from placing pieces on set S). We should choose S to maximize total ops, but the pieces placed then themselves get processed.\n\nLet f(x) = max total operations from a single piece starting on vertex x. Then f(x) = 1 + max over S of sum f(y) for y in S, subject to sum W_y < W_x, y adjacent to x.\n\nThis is a knapsack: for each vertex x, knapsack over neighbors y with weight W_y and value f(y), capacity W_x - 1.\n\nAnswer = sum A_i * f(i).\n\nBut f depends on other f's. We need ordering. Since sum W_y < W_x means W_x > sum >= max W_y (if S nonempty), so any y in S has W_y < W_x. So we can compute f in increasing order of W.\n\nWait, what about ties? If W_y = W_x, then W_y alone = W_x not < W_x, so can't include. So we only depend on vertices with strictly smaller W. Good, process in increasing W order.\n\nN=5000, M=5000. For each vertex x, knapsack with capacity W_x-1 <= 4999, items = neighbors with smaller W. Sum of degrees = 2M = 10000. Total work: sum over x of deg(x) * W_x <= 5000 * 5000 = 25M... actually sum deg(x)*W_x, worst case one vertex has degree ~100 with W=5000, but sum deg = 10000, so sum deg*W <= 10000 * 5000 = 5*10^7. Fine.\n\nLet me code it.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom sys import stdin\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N+1)]\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        v = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n    W = [0] + [int(input_data[idx+i]) for i in range(N)]\n    idx += N\n    A = [0] + [int(input_data[idx+i]) for i in range(N)]\n    idx += N\n    \n    order = sorted(range(1, N+1), key=lambda i: W[i])\n    f = [0] * (N+1)\n    \n    for x in order:\n        cap = W[x] - 1\n        # knapsack over neighbors with W[y] < W[x]\n        dp = [0] * (cap + 1)\n        for y in adj[x]:\n            if W[y] < W[x]:\n                w = W[y]\n                val = f[y]\n                # 0/1 knapsack\n                for c in range(cap, w-1, -1):\n                    nv = dp[c-w] + val\n                    if nv > dp[c]:\n                        dp[c] = nv\n        f[x] = 1 + max(dp) if cap >= 0 else 1\n    \n    ans = sum(A[i] * f[i] for i in range(1, N+1))\n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
