      "generated_answer": "<think>\nUse stack: iterate points 1..2N, for each point either push or pop match. Two chords intersect iff their intervals cross. Use stack: assign each chord's endpoints. When we encounter a point, if stack top is its pair, pop, else push. At end stack empty means no intersection.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    pair = [0] * (2*N + 1)\n    for _ in range(N):\n        a = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        b = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        pair[a] = b\n        pair[b] = a\n    stack = []\n    for i in range(1, 2*N+1):\n        if stack and stack[-1] == i:\n            stack.pop()\n        else:\n            stack.append(pair[i])\n    print(\"No\" if not stack else \"Yes\")\n\nmain()\n```",
