    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nEach position must be covered by some operation whose T alignment matches S at that position. A position i can be the start of an operation if S[i:i+M] == T, OR the operation extends beyond... wait, operations must fit in X, so start positions are 0 to N-M.\n\nFor each valid start position p (where S[p:p+M] matches T), we can perform that operation. But later operations overwrite. We need to check if there's an ordering such that final result is S.\n\nThink reverse: peel off operations. Position i in S must be \"covered\" by some operation, meaning there exists a start p with p<=i<p+M and T[i-p] == S[i]. But also, the last operation covering position i determines S[i].\n\nReverse process: start with S, repeatedly find a window of M consecutive positions that either match T or are already \"#\" (removed), and mark them as #. Can we reduce to all #?\n\nActually: find window [p, p+M) where for each position in window, either it's # or S[position] == T[position-p]. Then set all to #. Continue until all are #.\n\nThis is a greedy/BFS. N up to 2e5, M up to 5. \n\nApproach: BFS/queue. A position p can be \"removed\" (window starting at p applied last-among-remaining) if all positions in [p,p+M) match. After removal, those become wildcards, enabling more windows.\n\nUse a set of removable windows. When a position becomes wildcard, check windows containing it.\n\nLet me code: array state[i] = S[i] initially, or '#' if removed. A window at p is valid if for all j in [0,M): state[p+j]=='#' or state[p+j]==T[j].\n\nInitially find all valid windows. Process queue: pop a valid window, mark positions as '#', for each newly-# position, check windows that contain it (M windows) and add if newly valid and not already processed.\n\nCheck at end if all positions are '#'.\n\nWait but we need every position covered by at least one operation. If all positions become '#' through this process, yes.\n\nActually a position that never matched any T offset can never be covered — it would fail. Let me verify: if state[i] is 'A' and never becomes # via a window removal, then no window ever \"wrote\" S[i] as last-write. Correct.\n\nLet me implement.\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N, M = int(input_data[0]), int(input_data[1])\n    S = list(input_data[2])\n    T = input_data[3]\n    \n    def valid(p):\n        for j in range(M):\n            c = S[p+j]\n            if c != '#' and c != T[j]:\n                return False\n        return True\n    \n    in_queue = [False]*(N-M+1)\n    q = deque()\n    for p in range(N-M+1):\n        if valid(p):\n            q.append(p)\n            in_queue[p] = True\n    \n    while q:\n        p = q.popleft()\n        in_queue[p] = False\n        if not valid(p):\n            continue\n        changed = []\n        for j in range(M):\n            if S[p+j] != '#':\n                S[p+j] = '#'\n                changed.append(p+j)\n        for pos in changed:\n            for p2 in range(max(0, pos-M+1), min(N-M, pos)+1):\n                if not in_queue[p2] and valid(p2):\n                    in_queue[p2] = True\n                    q.append(p2)\n    \n    print(\"Yes\" if all(c=='#' for c in S) else \"No\")\n\nmain()\n```\n\nThe valid check is O(M)=O(5). Each position becomes # once. When a position changes, we check M windows, each O(M). Total O(N*M*M) = O(N*25) which is fine.\n\nOverall complexity acceptable.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N, M = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\n    S = list(data[2])\n    T = data[3]\n    \n    def valid(p):\n        for j in range(M):\n            c = S[p+j]\n            if c != '#' and c != T[j]:\n                return False\n        return True\n    \n    num_windows = N - M + 1\n    in_queue = [False]*num_windows\n    q = deque()\n    for p in range(num_windows):\n        if valid(p):\n            q.append(p)\n            in_queue[p] = True\n    \n    while q:\n        p = q.popleft()\n        in_queue[p] = False\n        if not valid(p):\n            continue\n        changed = []\n        for j in range(M):\n            if S[p+j] != '#':\n                S[p+j] = '#'\n                changed.append(p+j)\n        for pos in changed:\n            lo = max(0, pos-M+1)\n            hi = min(num_windows-1, pos)\n            for p2 in range(lo, hi+1):\n                if not in_queue[p2] and valid(p2):\n                    in_queue[p2] = True\n                    q.append(p2)\n    \n    print(\"Yes\" if all(c=='#' for c in S) else \"No\")\n\nmain()\n```",
