      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each person x_i, mark max y among insurances at that node. Then BFS/DFS from root: propagate max(y-1, child's own y). Count nodes with y>=0.\n\nSince parent index < child index, we can process in order 1..N. For each i, best[i] = max of insurance y's at i. Then for i from 1 to N: if best[i] >= 0, and for children... actually simpler: process in order, for each node compute effective coverage = max(own_y, parent_coverage - 1). If parent_coverage >=1 then child gets parent_coverage-1.\n\nLet me use -1 as \"not covered\". For node 1: cov[1] = best[1] (or -1). For i>=2: cov[i] = max(best[i], cov[p_i]-1). Count cov[i] >= 0.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    parent = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        parent[i] = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    best = [-1] * (N + 1)\n    for _ in range(M):\n        x = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        y = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        if y > best[x]:\n            best[x] = y\n    cov = [-1] * (N + 1)\n    cov[1] = best[1]\n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        c = cov[parent[i]] - 1\n        if best[i] > c:\n            c = best[i]\n        cov[i] = c\n    ans = sum(1 for i in range(1, N + 1) if cov[i] >= 0)\n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
