ction we came from.\n\nLet me redo: Start with cur = X, dist_up = 0. Contribution: f(X, K).\nThen loop: prev = cur, cur = cur//2, dist_up += 1. If cur == 0 break (means prev was 1). Remaining distance = K - dist_up. If remaining < 0 break.\n- Add 1 if remaining == 0 (cur itself).\n- Else: sibling = prev XOR 1. If sibling <= N and sibling != prev (i.e., prev != 1... well prev=1 means cur=0 already handled). Add f(sibling, remaining - 1).\n\nWait, also need prev != cur's only child case: if prev is the only child (sibling > N), skip.\n\nAlso when remaining == 0, we add cur (1 node). When remaining >= 1, we add nodes in sibling's subtree at depth remaining-1.\n\nLet me verify with sample: N=10, X=2, K=2.\nf(2,2) = subtree of 2 at depth 2: 2*4=8, range [8,11]∩[1,10]=[8,10] = 3. \nGo up: prev=2, cur=1, dist_up=1, remaining=1. remaining!=0, sibling=3, f(3,0)=1. Total so far 3+1=4. \nGo up: prev=1, cur=0, break. Answer 4. ✓\n\nK=1: f(2,1)= [4,5]=2. Up: cur=1, remaining=0, add 1. Total 3. ✓\n\nK=3: f(2,3)= 2*8=16>10, so 0. Up: cur=1, remaining=2, sibling=3, f(3,1)=[6,7]=2. Total 2. ✓\n\nK=0: f(2,0)=1. Up: cur=1, remaining=-1, break. Total 1. ✓\n\nGreat.\n\nNeed efficient f(v,d): if v > N or v*2^d > N (overflow risk with large d)... N up to 1e18. Python handles big ints. But d can be up to N-1 = 1e18-1, so 2^d huge. We should break early if v*2^d > N, return 0.\n\nActually simpler: if d is large enough that 2^d > N, then v*2^d > N (since v>=1), return 0. So cap: if d > 60 or so, likely 0. Check v * (1<<d) with d up to 62 max meaningfully.\n\nLet me code:\n\ndef f(v, d, N):\n    if v > N or d < 0: return 0\n    if d > 62: return 0  # 2^63 > 1e18\n    lo = v << d\n    if lo > N: return 0\n    hi = lo + (1 << d) - 1\n    return min(N, hi) - lo + 1\n\nMain loop iterates ~60 times (depth of X).\n\nLet me verify sample 2 first case: N=822981260158260522, X=52, K=20. Expected 1556480.\n\nI'll trust the logic.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    T = int(input_data[0])\n    idx = 1\n    out = []\n    for _ in range(T):\n        N = int(input_data[idx]); X = int(input_data[idx+1]); K = int(input_data[idx+2])\n        idx += 3\n        \n        def f(v, d):\n            if v > N or d < 0:\n                return 0\n            if d > 62:\n                return 0\n            lo = v << d\n            if lo > N:\n                return 0\n            hi = lo + (1 << d) - 1\n            if hi > N:\n                hi = N\n            return hi - lo + 1\n        \n        ans = f(X, K)\n        cur = X\n        dist_up = 0\n        while cur > 1:\n            prev = cur\n            cur = cur >> 1\n            dist_up += 1\n            remaining = K - dist_up\n            if remaining < 0:\n                break\n            if remaining == 0:\n                ans += 1\n            else:\n                sibling = prev ^ 1\n                if sibling <= N and sibling != prev:\n                    ans += f(sibling, remaining - 1)\n        \n        out.append(str(ans))\n    \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(out) + '\\n')\n\nsolve()\n```",
