    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each a from 1 to N-K+1, find positions of values a..a+K-1, then max-min. Use sliding window with sorted structure. \n\nActually, positions[v] = index of value v. For each window of K consecutive values, compute max(positions) - min(positions). Use a sorted multiset via SortedList, or use sliding window with monotonic deques for max and min.\n\nUse two deques for max and min over sliding window of positions[a..a+K-1].\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    K = int(input_data[1])\n    P = [int(x) for x in input_data[2:2+N]]\n    \n    pos = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i, v in enumerate(P):\n        pos[v] = i\n    \n    # sliding window over pos[1..N] of size K, find min of (max - min)\n    max_dq = deque()  # indices (values a) with decreasing pos\n    min_dq = deque()  # increasing pos\n    \n    ans = float('inf')\n    for a in range(1, N + 1):\n        p = pos[a]\n        while max_dq and pos[max_dq[-1]] <= p:\n            max_dq.pop()\n        max_dq.append(a)\n        while min_dq and pos[min_dq[-1]] >= p:\n            min_dq.pop()\n        min_dq.append(a)\n        \n        # window is [a-K+1, a]\n        left = a - K + 1\n        if left >= 1:\n            while max_dq[0] < left:\n                max_dq.popleft()\n            while min_dq[0] < left:\n                min_dq.popleft()\n            diff = pos[max_dq[0]] - pos[min_dq[0]]\n            if diff < ans:\n                ans = diff\n    \n    print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```",
