    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_92",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given two strings s and t of equal length n. You can perform the following operation on the string s:\n\nRemove a suffix of s of length l where 0 < l < n and append it at the start of s.\n\tFor example, let s = 'abcd' then in one operation you can remove the suffix 'cd' and append it in front of s making s = 'cdab'.\n\nYou are also given an integer k. Return the number of ways in which s can be transformed into t in exactly k operations.\nSince the answer can be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"abcd\", t = \"cdab\", k = 2\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: \nFirst way:\nIn first operation, choose suffix from index = 3, so resulting s = \"dabc\".\nIn second operation, choose suffix from index = 3, so resulting s = \"cdab\".\n\nSecond way:\nIn first operation, choose suffix from index = 1, so resulting s = \"bcda\".\nIn second operation, choose suffix from index = 1, so resulting s = \"cdab\".\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"ababab\", t = \"ababab\", k = 1\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: \nFirst way:\nChoose suffix from index = 2, so resulting s = \"ababab\".\n\nSecond way:\nChoose suffix from index = 4, so resulting s = \"ababab\".\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= s.length <= 5 * 10^5\n1 <= k <= 10^15\ns.length == t.length\ns and t consist of only lowercase English alphabets.",
    "prediction": "claude-opus-4-7",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nEach operation is a rotation. After k operations, we get some rotation of s. Let rotation by r mean the string starting at index r of original s (or think: one op with suffix length l transforms s to s[n-l:]+s[:n-l], which is rotation left by n-l, i.e., rotation index shifts by (n-l) mod n, where n-l ∈ {1,...,n-1}, so shift by any value in 1..n-1.\n\nSo each step shifts current rotation by some d ∈ {1,...,n-1} (mod n). Number of sequences of k such shifts that sum to r mod n.\n\nLet f(k, r) = number of ways to have sum ≡ r (mod n) with k terms each in {1,...,n-1}.\n\nRecurrence: total sequences = (n-1)^k. By symmetry, if r=0: a_k, else b_k (same for all nonzero r).\na_k + (n-1)*b_k = (n-1)^k.\na_k = (n-1)*b_{k-1} (previous must be nonzero, and last step brings back... wait).\n\nActually: a_k = number of ways sum ≡0. Recurrence: a_k = sum over last step d, previous sum ≡ -d. If d≠0 always. So a_k = sum_{d=1}^{n-1} f(k-1, -d mod n) = sum over nonzero residues = (n-1)^(k-1) - a_{k-1}... wait total is (n-1)^(k-1), minus f(k-1, 0) = a_{k-1}. So a_k = (n-1)^(k-1) - a_{k-1}.\n\nSimilarly b_k for r≠0: b_k = f(k-1, 0) + sum_{d≠0, d≠r} f(k-1, r-d). = a_{k-1} + (n-2)*b_{k-1}. Or use: a_k + (n-1)b_k = (n-1)^k, so b_k = ((n-1)^k - a_k)/(n-1).\n\nSolve a_k: a_k + a_{k-1} = (n-1)^{k-1}, with a_0 = 1 (empty sum ≡ 0).\n\nClosed form: a_k = ((n-1)^k + (-1)^k*(n-1))/n. Let me verify: a_0 = (1 + n-1)/n = 1. ✓\na_1 = (n-1 - (n-1))/n = 0. ✓ (one step can't give 0)\na_2 = ((n-1)^2 + (n-1))/n = (n-1)*n/n = n-1. ✓ (each nonzero d paired with n-d).\n\nSo a_k = ((n-1)^k + (-1)^k*(n-1)) / n\nb_k = ((n-1)^k - (-1)^k) / n\n\nNow find all rotations r such that rotating s by r gives t. For each such r, add a_k if r==0 else b_k.\n\nTo find valid rotations: concatenate s+s and find occurrences of t using KMP or Z-algorithm in first n positions.\n\nDivision by n: modular inverse.\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef solve(s, t, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Find all rotations r in [0, n-1] such that s rotated left by r equals t\n    # i.e., s[r:] + s[:r] == t, which means t appears at position r in s+s\n    ss = s + s\n    # KMP to find occurrences of t in ss[0:2n-1]\n    # Build failure function for pattern t\n    pat = t + '#' + ss[:2*n-1]  # actually just search\n    # Use KMP directly\n    def kmp_occurrences(text, pattern):\n        m = len(pattern)\n        fail = [0]*m\n        j = 0\n        for i in range(1, m):\n            while j > 0 and pattern[i] != pattern[j]:\n                j = fail[j-1]\n            if pattern[i] == pattern[j]:\n                j += 1\n            fail[i] = j\n        occ = []\n        j = 0\n        for i in range(len(text)):\n            while j > 0 and text[i] != pattern[j]:\n                j = fail[j-1]\n            if text[i] == pattern[j]:\n                j += 1\n            if j == m:\n                occ.append(i - m + 1)\n                j = fail[j-1]\n        return occ\n    \n    occs = kmp_occurrences(ss[:2*n-1] if 2*n-1 >= n else ss, t)\n    valid_zero = 0  # count of r == 0 valid\n    valid_nonzero = 0  # count of r != 0 valid\n    for r in occs:\n        if 0 <= r < n:\n            if r == 0:\n                valid_zero = 1\n            else:\n                valid_nonzero += 1\n    \n    # a_k = ((n-1)^k + (-1)^k * (n-1)) / n\n    # b_k = ((n-1)^k - (-1)^k) / n\n    pw = pow(n-1, k, MOD)\n    sign = 1 if k % 2 == 0 else MOD - 1\n    inv_n = pow(n, MOD-2, MOD)\n    a_k = (pw + sign * (n-1)) % MOD * inv_n % MOD\n    b_k = (pw - sign) % MOD * inv_n % MOD\n    \n    ans = (valid_zero * a_k + valid_nonzero * b_k) % MOD\n    return ans\n```",
