      "generated_answer": "<think>\nFor each cell, check if starting there, all moves stay on land. Count valid ending positions.\n</think>\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    H = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    W = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    T = input_data[idx]; idx+=1\n    S = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        S.append(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    \n    dmap = {'L':(0,-1),'R':(0,1),'U':(-1,0),'D':(1,0)}\n    \n    ends = set()\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if S[i][j] != '.':\n                continue\n            r, c = i, j\n            ok = True\n            for ch in T:\n                dr, dc = dmap[ch]\n                r += dr; c += dc\n                if r < 0 or r >= H or c < 0 or c >= W or S[r][c] != '.':\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            if ok:\n                ends.add((r,c))\n    print(len(ends))\n\nmain()\n```",
