      "generated_answer": "<think>\nBFS on bipartite graph sets-elements. Find shortest path from any set containing 1 to any set containing M. Answer is (number of sets in path) - 1. BFS distance from element 1: distance to element M in bipartite... \n\nActually, model: nodes = sets and elements. Edge between set and each element in it. BFS from element 1 to element M. Path length is 2k, meaning k sets used, answer k-1.\n\nIf 1 and M in same set, answer 0.\n\nLet me BFS from node \"element 1\", find shortest distance to \"element M\". Distance is 2k where k = number of sets on path. Answer = k-1.\n</think>\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n    \n    # nodes: sets 0..N-1, elements N..N+M-1 (element e -> N+e-1)\n    set_adj = [[] for _ in range(N)]\n    elem_adj = [[] for _ in range(M+1)]  # 1..M\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        A = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n        for _ in range(A):\n            e = int(input_data[idx]); idx+=1\n            set_adj[i].append(e)\n            elem_adj[e].append(i)\n    \n    # Check if any set contains both 1 and M\n    for i in range(N):\n        s = set_adj[i]\n        has1 = 1 in s\n        hasM = M in s\n        if has1 and hasM:\n            print(0)\n            return\n    \n    # BFS from element 1 to element M\n    # dist to elements\n    INF = -1\n    elem_dist = [INF]*(M+1)\n    set_dist = [INF]*N\n    \n    if not elem_adj[1] or not elem_adj[M]:\n        print(-1)\n        return\n    \n    elem_dist[1] = 0\n    q = deque([('e', 1)])\n    while q:\n        typ, node = q.popleft()\n        if typ == 'e':\n            d = elem_dist[node]\n            for s in elem_adj[node]:\n                if set_dist[s] == INF:\n                    set_dist[s] = d+1\n                    if s == -1: pass\n                    q.append(('s', s))\n        else:\n            d = set_dist[node]\n            for e in set_adj[node]:\n                if elem_dist[e] == INF:\n                    elem_dist[e] = d+1\n                    if e == M:\n                        # number of sets = elem_dist[M] (which is 2k, k sets)\n                        # Wait: elem_dist counts steps. elem 1 -> set -> elem -> set -> ... -> elem M\n                        # distance in edges = 2k where k sets used\n                        # answer = k-1\n                        k = elem_dist[M]//2\n                        print(k-1)\n                        return\n                    q.append(('e', e))\n    \n    print(-1)\n\nmain()\n```",
