      "generated_answer": "NaCl's validator forbids any instruction that modifies x86 segment state (since segments enforce the sandbox), and forbids indirect jumps unless they are preceded by the and-mask alignment pseudo-instruction that forces the target to a 32-byte boundary. Indirect loads/stores are allowed (segmentation handles them), and unaligned loads/stores aren't forbidden per se — only unaligned control flow is.\n\n\\boxed{A, D}",
