      "generated_answer": "The linear regression estimator (ordinary least squares) has the smallest variance among all linear unbiased estimators, not all unbiased estimators, so Statement 1 is false. In AdaBoost, the coefficients α are always non-negative because they are computed as \\( \\alpha_t = \\frac{1}{2} \\ln\\left(\\frac{1-\\varepsilon_t}{\\varepsilon_t}\\right) \\), and \\( \\varepsilon_t < 0.5 \\) ensures positivity, while \\( \\varepsilon_t = 0.5 \\) gives zero; thus Statement 2 is true. Therefore, the correct choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
