      "generated_answer": "Reporting a child's genuine criminal behavior to authorities—especially when they are already on probation and have a history of escalating offenses—is a morally defensible act of accountability and potentially life-saving intervention. The parent is not fabricating anything; the son actually committed fraud, and shielding him would enable further harm. Therefore, the parent would NOT be the asshole for reporting.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
