    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "<think>\nYen put on dollars with strike ¥125 corresponds via currency option duality.\n\nDollar put on yen: strike $0.008, spot $0.011, price $0.0005.\nThis is right to sell yen for $0.008, i.e., buy dollars... \n\nUse the relationship: P_$(x0, K, T) in dollars relates to yen-denominated call on dollars.\n\nActually: A dollar-denominated put on yen with strike K gives right to sell 1 yen for K dollars. Equivalently, right to buy K dollars for 1 yen... this is a yen-denominated call on dollars.\n\nThe formula: P_$(x0, K) = x0 * K * C_¥(1/x0, 1/K)\n\nSo $0.0005 = 0.011 * 0.008 ",
