      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is E, as urbanization and the pursuit of better economic opportunities, shorter hours, and improved social amenities in cities are well-documented drivers of the relative shift away from farming. Other options, such as automation or disease, may have localized effects but do not universally explain the global trend. Thus, E captures the common socioeconomic reasons for rural-to-urban migration.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
