ht mean torus contains sphere? Problem says internal—typo probably. r_i when sphere inside torus hole: distance =11-3=8, r_i=33/4.\n\nr_i - r_o = 33/4 - 33/7 = 33(7-4)/28 = 99/28. gcd(99,28)=1. Answer 127.\n</think>\n\n**Answer:** Setting the sphere center at origin and torus axis vertical, tube center circle at distance 6 from axis and height h. For tangency, distance from origin to tube center = 11±3.\n\n- Internal case (distance = 8): tangent circle radius $r_i = 6 \\cdot \\frac{11}{8} = \\frac{33}{4}$\n- External case (distance = 14): tangent circle radius $r_o = 6 \\cdot \\frac{11}{14} = \\frac{33}{7}$\n\nThus $r_i - r_o = \\frac{33}{4} - \\frac{33}{7} = \\frac{99}{28}$, giving $m+n = 99+28$.\n\n\\boxed{127}",
