      "generated_answer": "<think>\nS_n = sum over k of k * (number of pairs with |A∩B|=k, |A|=|B|).\n\nStandard result: S_n = n * C(2n-1, n-1). Let me verify for n=2: 2*C(3,1)=2*3=6. Not 4.\n\nLet me recompute. S_n = sum_{|A|=|B|} |A∩B|. \n\n|A∩B| = sum_i [i∈A][i∈B]. So S_n = sum_i sum_{|A|=|B|, i∈A, i∈B} 1 = n * (number of pairs A,B with |A|=|B| both containing element 1).\n\nNumber of pairs with |A|=|B|=k both containing 1: C(n-1,k-1)^2. Sum over k=1..n: sum C(n-1,k-1)^2 = C(2n-2, n-1).\n\nSo S_n = n * C(2n-2, n-1).\n\nCheck n=2: 2*C(2,1) = 2*2 = 4. ✓\n\nS_2022/S_2021 = [2022 * C(4042, 2021)] / [2021 * C(4040, 2020)].\n\nC(4042,2021)/C(4040,2020) = [4042!/(2021!2021!)] / [4040!/(2020!2020!)] = 4041*4042/(2021*2021) = 4041*4042/2021².\n\nNote 4042 = 2*2021, so = 4041*2*2021/2021² = 2*4041/2021 = 8082/2021.\n\nSo ratio = (2022/2021) * (8082/2021) = 2022*8082/2021².\n\n2021² = 2021*2021. 2022*8082 = 2022*8082.\n\nCheck gcd. 2021 = 43*47. 2022 = 2*3*337. 8082 = 2*4041 = 2*3*1347 = 2*3*3*449 = 2*9*449. gcd with 2021: 2021 shares nothing with 2022 or 8082? 449 prime? 449/43 no, /47 no. 337 prime, not 43 or 47. So gcd(2022*8082, 2021²)=1.\n\np = 2022*8082, q = 2021².\n2022*8082 = 2022*8082. 2022*8000=16176000, 2022*82=165804, total=16341804.\n2021² = 4084441.\np+q = 16341804 + 4084441 = 20426245.\nMod 1000: 245.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nUsing $|A \\cap B| = \\sum_i [i \\in A][i \\in B]$ and symmetry, $S_n = n \\cdot C(2n-2, n-1)$ (verified: $S_2 = 2 \\cdot 2 = 4$). \n\nThen $\\frac{S_{2022}}{S_{2021}} = \\frac{2022 \\cdot C(4042,2021)}{2021 \\cdot C(4040,2020)} = \\frac{2022 \\cdot 4041 \\cdot 4042}{2021 \\cdot 2021^2} = \\frac{2022 \\cdot 8082}{2021^2} = \\frac{16341804}{4084441}$, which is already in lowest terms since $2021 = 43 \\cdot 47$ shares no factors with the numerator.\n\nThus $p+q = 20426245$, giving remainder $\\boxed{245}$.",
