      "generated_answer": "The correct method for estimating the age of a rock using radioactive elements is radiometric dating, which measures the decay of parent isotopes into daughter isotopes. Option G correctly describes this by referencing the proportion of uranium and lead to determine absolute age. Other options, such as fossil content or density, do not rely on radioactive decay.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
