    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The end-replication problem occurs because DNA polymerases need a primer and synthesize 5'→3', leaving the ends incompletely replicated. Retroviruses solve this through their reverse transcription mechanism, which uses template switching and the LTRs (long terminal repeats) to ensure the ends are fully copied — effectively copying the 5' end information before completing the strand.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
